    id: 10016,
    title: "How to Choose NFL Jerseys: Sizing, Styles and Player vs Custom",
    slug: "how-to-choose-nfl-jerseys-sizing-styles",
    excerpt: "Game jersey or custom? Stitched or screen-printed? Here's how to pick the right NFL jersey for fit, style and budget.",
    content: "Choosing an NFL jersey should be fun, but the options can overwhelm. Between game jerseys, limited editions and custom names, fans face a maze of styles and prices. Start with the fit: NFL jerseys run large by design, so most fans size down from their everyday shirt. Player jerseys celebrate a star, but custom jerseys let you wear your own name and favorite number — or a retired legend who never played for your team. Stitched numbers cost more but survive years of game day wear, while screen-printed versions are the budget pick. Buy from the team's official shop to avoid counterfeits, check the size guide before checkout, and remember that a jersey is only as good as the game day experience you pair it with at the best NFL stadiums across the country. Whether you are filling a team roster gap or just adding a classic to your collection, the right jersey turns any fan into a lifelong supporter.",
