    id: 10017,
    title: "The Ultimate NFL Tailgating Guide: Food, Games and Parking",
    slug: "ultimate-nfl-tailgating-guide-food-games-parking",
    excerpt: "Tailgating is an NFL ritual. From the grill to the cornhole boards, here's how to throw the ultimate pregame tailgate.",
    content: "Tailgating is the unofficial start of every NFL Sunday. Hours before kickoff, parking lots around the best NFL stadiums fill with grills, coolers and flags. The essentials: arrive early — lots open three to four hours before kickoff — and scout the parking rules online so your setup is legal. Food is the star: burgers, wings and dips cook while cornhole boards keep the crowd busy. Budget ticket prices alongside tailgate costs so game day fits your wallet, and pack layers — September and October weather swings fast. A good tailgate is about community: bring extra chairs, share your grill, and trade stories with fans in any jersey. By kickoff you will have made friends, eaten well and built the kind of game day experience that brings fans back season after season.",
