    id: 10023,
    title: "NFL Week 1 Fantasy Starts and Sits: Lineup Decisions That Win",
    slug: "nfl-week-1-fantasy-starts-and-sits-lineup-decisions",
    excerpt: "Week 1 fantasy football is the hardest week. These are the start-sit calls that separate champions from also-rans.",
    content: "Week 1 is the hardest week of the fantasy football season. You have no in-season data, just a full offseason of hype. The start-sit decisions you make on Thursday night can set the tone for your entire season. Start the workhorses: elite running backs with clear roles are safer than ever in Week 1, because coaches lean on established names before the depth chart settles. Sit the rookies on bad offenses even if rookie rankings loved them, and check every injury report before kickoff for surprise inactives. Stream the waiver wire aggressively in week one — the best fantasy sleepers emerge exactly here, when owners overreact to one bad game. Balance floor over ceiling, trust your quarterback rankings over matchup anxiety, and remember that champions are built in the first four weeks of the season.",
